// ESP32-S3 port early app 08: unbounded recursion in `main`, which is not an actor and runs on the
// platform's stack (spec §15.1.2.2). Exhausting it is a fatal fault (§15.4.5.5), reported the same way
// on every target: "[silica] fault at 0x<pc>..." and exit status 70. On the host the SIGSEGV on the
// guard page reaches the runtime's handler on its alternate stack; on the board the stack-guard data
// breakpoint raises a debug exception (the board-only details after the exit marker say
// "exccause=1006 ... (stack guard"). Nothing is printed before the fault. The addresses differ by run
// and target: compare with tools/compare_sout.sh (board) or the ladder's normalized diff.
fn down(n: int64) -> int64 {
    1 + down(n + 1)
}

fn main() -> int64 { down(0) }
